{"name":"Wolfram","hex":"#b5b6b7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wolfram","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["wolframite","tungsten"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wolfram"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wolfram (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Wolfram is a 2025 Australian Western drama film directed by Warwick Thornton. It is a sequel to Thornton's 2017 film Sweet Country, reprising several of the same characters. It stars Deborah Mailman, Pedrea Jackson, Thomas M. Wright and Luka May Glynn-Cole. The title refers to the Hatches Creek wolfram field in the Northern Territory, where Aboriginal Australian children were exploited for their labour, digging tungsten out of the ground."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Wolfram_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfram_(film)","wikidata":"Q136376941"},{"title":"Wolfram (musician)","blocks":[{"text":"Wolfram Eckert, known professionally as Wolfram, is an Austrian electronic dance music disc jockey and record producer. His style includes Italo disco and Eurodance and he is known as a DJ in the fashion industry. He also works under the alias Diskokaine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/WOLFRAM_ANALOG.jpg/330px-WOLFRAM_ANALOG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfram_(musician)","wikidata":"Q16937965"},{"title":"Wolfram (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Wolfram is both a given name and surname of Germanic origin. It is composed as wolf ‘wolf’ + hrafn ‘raven’, important in Germanic mythology."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfram_(name)","wikidata":"Q847566"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/George_Bastian_084.tif/lossy-page1-500px-George_Bastian_084.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten